I go near the entrance.
There is a large wooden counter there.
I stand near the counter.
An elderly man sits behind the counter.
He is near the cash register.
I look at him.
I greet him respectfully.
I say, "Namaste chacha."
He looks at me.
He also smiles.
He says, "Namaste."
Now I look on the counter.
There is a glass on the counter.
Under the glass is a menu.
It is a handwritten menu.
I read that menu carefully.
There are many items there.
I think for a moment.
